# Checkout line endings are part of what CI executes, so they are pinned here
# rather than left to each machine's core.autocrlf setting.
#
# Two failures in this repository came from this: a Windows checkout that
# converts a shell script to CRLF cannot run it (`bash` rejects the trailing
# `\r` on the first real line), and a workflow file read as text no longer
# matches the step markers the release tests look for. Both were worked around
# in the reader; this file removes the cause.
#
# PowerShell is deliberately not listed: Windows PowerShell and PowerShell 7
# accept either ending, and a CRLF checkout is what a Windows author expects.
# Binary assets are not listed either, so nothing is renormalised by accident.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf
*.nsi  text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.go   text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.ts   text eol=lf
*.tsx  text eol=lf
*.css  text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
